,title,link,text,language,family
0,Pazeh–Kaxabu language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pazeh–Kaxabu_language,"Pazeh (also spelled Pazih, Pazéh) and Kaxabu are dialects of a Formosan language of the Austronesian language family. It is the original language of the Pazeh and Kaxabu, neighboring Taiwanese indigenous peoples.",Pazeh,Austronesian
1,The Prosodic Structure of Pazeh - Western University,https://www.uwo.ca/linguistics/afla26/abstracts/Macaulay_AFLA_26_paper_8.pdf,"This paper presents novel data on the prosody and intonation of Pazeh, an Austronesian language of Taiwan declared extinct in 2010. The discovery of an additional speaker has allowed for continued documentation of the language.",Pazeh,Austronesian
2,Pazeh language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/Pazeh_language,"Pazeh, also known as Pazih, is classified as a Formosan language within the Austronesian language family, representing one of the indigenous languages of Taiwan originating from the western plains.",Pazeh,Austronesian
3,Pazeh and Kaxabu - ling.sinica.edu.tw,https://www.ling.sinica.edu.tw/upload/researcher_manager_result/b70c4dafb5fed1963fb8bb94a1944a1c.pdf,"Pazeh is still spoken by a few speakers, but the exact number is not currently known; Kaxabu is spoken to some extent by about 10 people over 70 years old (as of May 2021 ).",Pazeh,Austronesian
4,Austronesian Music - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/@austronesianmusic6149,"Hi everyone! Welcome to Austronesian Music🎶This channel mainly posts music from Austronesian countries and languages, and also other songs of languages of Southeast Asia.",Pazeh,Austronesian
5,Austronesian Music - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLnOSH5j1sQh9pFS_rqvm3r2JtCD8AGOa-,"Austronesian culture includes more than 1200 ethnic groups, across South Asia, Southeast Asia, Taiwan, the Philippines, parts of China, as well as the Pacifi...",Pazeh,Austronesian
6,Pazeh and Kaxabu,https://www.ling.sinica.edu.tw/upload/researcher_manager_result/1189e242663716673499512083d4ddd1.pdf,"The position of Pazeh and Kaxabu within the Austronesian phylogeny has not yet been definitively settled, and four different hypotheses have been given in the literature, namely, those of Li (1985), Blust (1999a, 1999b), and Sagart",Pazeh,Austronesian
7,Microsoft Word - Austronesian music web.doc,https://rogerblench.info/Ethnomusicology/Papers/Asia/General/Blench+AN+music+paper+I.pdf,"If the original Austronesian homeland was in South China, then this highly unusual music was probably carried eastwards to Formosa at a very early period.Pazeh. libex. Proto-Rukai.",Pazeh,Austronesian
8,(PDF) The prosodic structure of Pazeh,https://www.academia.edu/45332078/The_prosodic_structure_of_Pazeh,"This paper presents novel data on the prosody and intonation of Pazeh, an Austronesian language of Taiwan thought to have lost its last speaker in 2010.",Pazeh,Austronesian
9,"Pazeh Language (PZH) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status... | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/pzh/,Pazeh is an endangered indigenous language of Taiwan. It belongs to the Austronesian language family. The language is used as a first language by the elderly only.,Pazeh,Austronesian
